From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: take the management ack header again after the pull

The handler takes mgmt_ethhdr from skb_mac_header() before pskb_may_pull()
and keeps using that pointer afterwards. pskb_may_pull() can move the
head, so read ->seq and ->mdio_data through a stale pointer. Take the
header again after the pull, as the MIB path already does.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -198,6 +198,9 @@
 	if (data_len && !pskb_may_pull(skb, data_len))
 		goto complete;
 
+	/* pskb_may_pull() can move the head; take the header again. */
+	mgmt_ethhdr = (struct qca_mgmt_ethhdr *)skb_mac_header(skb);
+
 	/* Make sure the seq match the requested packet */
 	if (get_unaligned_le32(&mgmt_ethhdr->seq) == mgmt_eth_data->seq)
 		mgmt_eth_data->ack = true;
